From 2111206d74a2eac12e824982391046400688e078 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
Date: Sun, 24 May 2026 16:12:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ec: propagate OTel parent trace context through EC read
 pipeline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds end-to-end propagation of jspan_context from RGW GET through
ECBackend to peer-OSD shard reads and BlueStore. Mirrors the existing
write-path machinery (RMWPipeline::Op already carries jspan_context).

Wire-format change:
  * MOSDECSubOpRead bumps HEAD_VERSION 3 -> 4 and encodes/decodes
    otel_trace alongside the existing blkin trace. Older OSDs that
    speak v3 ignore the field; v4+ peers pick it up via the generic
    OSD::dispatch path (OSD.cc:7753 already sets
    op->osd_parent_span from m->otel_trace for any incoming message).

API plumbing:
  * PGBackend::objects_read_async virtual gains an optional
    const jspan_context *parent_trace = nullptr.
  * ECSwitch::objects_read_async forwards parent_trace to ECBackend
    (optimized backend) and drops it for ECBackendL (legacy backend
    keeps its 5-arg form — propagation through ECBackendL's read
    pipeline is a separate effort).
  * ECBackend::objects_read_async -> objects_read_and_reconstruct
    -> read_pipeline.objects_read_and_reconstruct -> start_read_op
    threads parent_trace down to ReadOp.otel_ctx (new field that
    mirrors WriteOp::Op::otel_ctx).
  * ECCommon::ReadPipeline at the MOSDECSubOpRead build site sets
    msg->otel_trace = rop.otel_ctx so the peer OSD picks it up.
  * ECBackend::handle_sub_read gains a parent_trace param that the
    dispatcher derives from _op->osd_parent_span; the 2 local
    store->read sites for own-shard reads now pass parent_trace.
  * ReplicatedBackend::objects_read_async accepts parent_trace
    (signature-only, no behavior change — its sync path already
    propagates via objects_read_sync from the bluestore-read-subspans
    patch).
  * PrimaryLogPG::OpContext::start_async_reads materializes
    op->osd_parent_span->GetContext() and passes its address to
    pgbackend->objects_read_async.

Status: code is in place. End-to-end Tempo verification is pending
investigation of Tempo's WAL->block flush behavior — the cluster's
tempo instance currently shows total_blocks=0 in search responses,
so trace fragments visible via /api/traces/<id> aren't reliably
aggregating across services. Code review is welcome; behavior
verification will follow once Tempo is healthy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
